>I'm looking for tactical information for nethack. With tactical, I mean
>hints what to do or what not to do, as opposed to spoilers (of which
>I have MBs cluttering up my harddisk).
>
>For example I am interested in :
>	- How do you survive the Quest (or, even, the Gnomish Mines) safely?
>	- What is the best way of fighting a black dragon (or a mumak)?

That knowledge is very difficult to write down - it depends too much on your
level, stats, equipment and general tactical situation... That's what
experience is (and I mean experience, not XP). 

My strategy is as follows:
1) Don't go into the mines before you have a good chance of surviving them 
and that means that you can kill two dvarves attacking you at the same time
(and this could mean that you have mega-weapon, or good ofensive wand, or
intrinsic speed, or...). But do the mines as soon as you are strong enough
there are lots of goodies there...
2) If you have some means of scanning levels for monsters - do it whenever
entering any new level, this can save you many surprises.
3) Don't be ashamed if you run away... A very good strategy is to flee up
or down stairs, most monsters don't follow you. Try to always have an escape
route. A few teleport scrolls or a wand can help a lot.
4) Intrinsics can be life. Try to get them at any price. Speed, reflection,
telepathy, and even the lowly searching can extend your life span a lot.
5) Avoid using unidentified items, if you do at least check the curse
status first...

Youer specific questions - well, for the quest you have to be sure that you can
stand whatever monsters are generated in the quest. Depends on the character
cleass...
Black dragon/mumak - depends on your intrinsics/strength weapon. Generally
either attack frontally or run away. If you have a wall behing you - use 
your equipment (creatively :-)
